From: Remora <remora@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] vtest: align linear image row pitch to 256 bytes

A LINEAR image whose row pitch is not a multiple of 256 makes the GPU fault a
few frames into rendering:

    NVRM: Xid (PCI:0000:01:00): 69, name=vkr-ring-1, Class Error:
          channel 0x28, Class 0000c797, Offset 000019d0, ErrorCode 0000000f

0xc797 is the Ampere_B 3D class and vkr-ring-1 is this server's own Venus ring
thread, so the invalid 3D-class state is submitted host-side. The context is
lost, the guest's next fence poll can never succeed, and Venus hard-aborts in
vn_ring_submit_locked -- taking SurfaceFlinger's RenderEngine with it.
mesa.vn.debug=...,no_abort does not cover a ring-submit failure.

The failing variable is the pitch, not the size:

    1280 wide -> pitch  5120, %256 = 0    works
    1920 wide -> pitch  7680, %256 = 0    works
    3760 wide -> pitch 15040, %256 = 192  faults
    3840 wide -> pitch 15360, %256 = 0    clean, and LARGER than the failing case

vtest_gpu_alloc_image() reports whatever layout.rowPitch the driver returns,
while the udmabuf path beside it has always aligned with
ALLOC_ALIGN(width * bpp, 256) -- which is why only this path was affected. An
A/B differing only in routing confirms it: VTEST_MAPPABLE_GPU=1 faults,
VTEST_MAPPABLE_UDMABUF=1 does not.

Pad the width rather than forcing a pitch through
VkImageDrmFormatModifierExplicitCreateInfoEXT: the driver keeps ownership of
every other alignment rule, and the padded columns are never addressed because
the guest is told the real width alongside the reported stride.

Verified end to end at 3760x1992 through `remora up`: Xid 0, no RenderEngine
abort, and scrcpy reporting "Texture: 3760x1992".

---
 vtest/vtest_gpu_alloc.c | 24 +++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/vtest/vtest_gpu_alloc.c b/vtest/vtest_gpu_alloc.c
--- a/vtest/vtest_gpu_alloc.c
+++ b/vtest/vtest_gpu_alloc.c
@@ -313,12 +313,36 @@
       .drmFormatModifierCount = mod_count,
       .pDrmFormatModifiers = mod_candidates,
    };
+   /* LINEAR row pitch MUST land on 256 bytes or the GPU faults.
+    *
+    * An unaligned pitch produces, several frames later, an Xid 69 class error
+    * against the Ampere 3D class (Class 0000c797, Offset 000019d0) that kills
+    * this server's context; the guest then aborts in vn_ring_submit_locked
+    * while polling fence status, taking SurfaceFlinger's RenderEngine with it.
+    * It is NOT a size limit:
+    *   3760 wide -> pitch 15040, 15040 % 256 = 192 -> faults
+    *   3840 wide -> pitch 15360, 15360 % 256 =   0 -> clean, though LARGER
+    * The udmabuf path below has always aligned its stride to 256, which is why
+    * only this path was affected.
+    *
+    * Pad the WIDTH so the driver's own linear pitch comes out aligned, rather
+    * than forcing a pitch through an explicit-layout create: the padded columns
+    * are never addressed (the guest is told the real width and the reported
+    * stride), and letting the driver keep ownership of the layout avoids
+    * second-guessing its other alignment rules.
+    */
+   uint32_t alloc_width = width;
+   if (linear) {
+      const uint32_t bpp = drm_format_bpp(drm_format);
+      if (bpp)
+         alloc_width = (uint32_t)(ALLOC_ALIGN((uint64_t)width * bpp, 256) / bpp);
+   }
    const VkImageCreateInfo image_info = {
       .sType = VK_STRUCTURE_TYPE_IMAGE_CREATE_INFO,
       .pNext = &mod_info,
       .imageType = VK_IMAGE_TYPE_2D,
       .format = format,
-      .extent = { width, height, 1 },
+      .extent = { alloc_width, height, 1 },
       .mipLevels = 1,
       .arrayLayers = 1,
       .samples = VK_SAMPLE_COUNT_1_BIT,
